    "turn_type_label": "Substantive"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 80224,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/0/80224.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 13,
    "turn_text": "Well, I think that we've got major problems in regard to healthcare. We've got 44 million people who are uninsured. And that number may even double if you talk to healthcare professionals when you factor in the folks who are underinsured or the people who are in part-time or temporary positions because they come in and out of employment. So it may be as much as 80 million people who are unemployed. This not only creates a situation where folks don't have health coverage, but it also increases the cost that those who are insured have to pay for their health care. I think we have to make some major changes in our health care and we need to make quality affordable health care accessible to everyone.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "There are major problems in regard to healthcare.",
        "confidence": 0.97
      },
      {
        "text": "Major changes are needed in the current healthcare system.",
        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "44 million people in the U.S. are uninsured.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "Affordable and high-quality healthcare should be accessible to everyone.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "Lack of universal health coverage increases costs for those who are insured.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "The number of people without adequate healthcare could rise to 80 million when including the underinsured and those in unstable employment.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "People in part-time or temporary jobs often lack consistent health insurance.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "Healthcare access is a fundamental right or moral imperative.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "Economic instability leads to gaps in health insurance coverage.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "Underinsurance is a meaningful form of healthcare insecurity comparable to being fully uninsured.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Systemic healthcare inequities contribute directly to rising costs for all consumers.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker’s definition of 'uninsured' includes broader forms of vulnerability beyond formal policy status.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      },
      {
        "text": "Policy intervention can effectively address systemic healthcare disparities.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      },
      {
        "text": "Healthcare affordability and accessibility are interconnected and mutually reinforcing goals.",
        "confidence": 0.86
      },
      {
        "text": "The audience accepts the premise that large-scale healthcare issues require structural reform.",
        "confidence": 0.85
